FINANCE/PHYSICAL CLOSURE. The new Codex finance work correctly records token dimensions, but FreeToken exposes why token counts alone are insufficient for local/open-weight economics.

Extend the canonical UsageOccurrence detail vocabulary (optional, evidenced, never zero-filled) so local inference can record where available:
- prefill/decode tokens and reused-prefix tokens;
- expert cache hits/misses/fills/evictions;
- host bytes read, PCIe bytes transferred, CPU-executed expert bytes, GPU-executed expert bytes;
- measured B_P/B_H and calibration profile ref;
- wall time split by prefill/decode/transfer/CPU/GPU;
- VRAM budget, KV bytes/pages, expert-cache bytes/slots, cache resize events;
- model weight representation/precision and checkpoint/body refs;
- energy/power only when actually measured.

EconomicMeasure may price electricity, amortized hardware, or provider usage only from versioned evidence. Unknown local cost remains unknown. Avoided transfer/recompute is an efficiency delta, not automatically cash savings.

Expose through the same semantic shell: @work/... |> ?realizations |> ?usage |> ?economics |> ?evidence.
